        "where the first term captures systematic market risk and the second term captures idiosyncratic risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Exercise 3\n",
        "\n",
        "Using the true mean vector $\\mu$ and covariance matrix $\\Sigma$ constructed in Exercise 2, we implement functions to compute the tangency portfolio and the mean–variance efficient frontier.\n",
        "\n",
        "The efficient frontier consists of portfolios that minimize portfolio variance for a given target return,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\omega_{eff}(\\bar{\\mu})\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\arg\\min_{\\omega}\n",
        "\\omega' \\Sigma \\omega,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "subject to\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\omega' \\iota = 1,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\omega' \\mu \\ge \\bar{\\mu}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The tangency portfolio is computed as\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\omega_{tan}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{\\Sigma^{-1}\\tilde{\\mu}}\n",
        "{\\iota' \\Sigma^{-1}\\tilde{\\mu}},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "where $\\tilde{\\mu} = \\mu-r_f$ denotes expected excess returns.\n",
        "\n",
        "The implemented functions return portfolio weights together with the corresponding expected return, variance, volatility and Sharpe ratio. They are used throughout the remainder of the assignment to evaluate portfolio allocations under both true and estimated parameters."
      ],
      "id": "04754644"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| label: ex3-frontier-functions\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_tangency_portfolio(mu, Sigma):\n",
        "    inv_Sigma = np.linalg.inv(Sigma)\n",
        "\n",
        "    weights = inv_Sigma @ mu\n",
        "    weights = weights / np.sum(weights)\n",
        "\n",
        "    portfolio_mean = weights @ mu\n",
        "    portfolio_variance = weights @ Sigma @ weights\n",
        "    portfolio_volatility = np.sqrt(portfolio_variance)\n",
        "    portfolio_sharpe = portfolio_mean / portfolio_volatility\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"weights\": weights,\n",
        "        \"mean\": portfolio_mean,\n",
        "        \"variance\": portfolio_variance,\n",
        "        \"volatility\": portfolio_volatility,\n",
        "        \"sharpe\": portfolio_sharpe\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_efficient_frontier(mu, Sigma, n_points=100):\n",
        "    ones = np.ones(len(mu))\n",
        "    inv_Sigma = np.linalg.inv(Sigma)\n",
        "\n",
        "    A = ones @ inv_Sigma @ ones\n",
        "    B = ones @ inv_Sigma @ mu\n",
        "    C = mu @ inv_Sigma @ mu\n",
        "    D = A * C - B**2\n",
        "\n",
        "    target_returns = np.linspace(mu.min(), mu.max(), n_points)\n",
        "    frontier = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for target_return in target_returns:\n",
        "        weights = inv_Sigma @ (\n",
        "            ((C - B * target_return) / D) * ones\n",
        "            + ((A * target_return - B) / D) * mu\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        portfolio_variance = weights @ Sigma @ weights\n",
        "        portfolio_volatility = np.sqrt(portfolio_variance)\n",
        "\n",
        "        frontier.append({\n",
        "            \"target_return\": target_return,\n",
        "            \"volatility\": portfolio_volatility,\n",
        "            \"variance\": portfolio_variance\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(frontier)"
      ],
      "id": "ex3-frontier-functions",
