        "## Exercise 6\n",
        "To evaluate the impact of estimation error on portfolio performance, we compare the true tangency portfolio with the plug-in tangency portfolio. The plug-in portfolio is constructed from the estimated moments $\\hat{\\mu}$ and $\\hat{\\Sigma}$, but its Sharpe ratio is evaluated using the true parameters $\\mu$ and $\\Sigma$.\n",
        "\n",
        "The out-of-sample Sharpe ratio is computed as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "SR(w)=\\frac{w^\\top \\mu}{\\sqrt{w^\\top \\Sigma w}}.\n",
        "$$"
